```

This implementation uses two heaps to maintain the two halves of the sorted list of numbers. The `max_heap` stores the smaller half of the numbers using negative values to simulate a max heap with Python's `heapq`, which is a min heap by default. The `min_heap` stores the larger half. This ensures that the median can be found efficiently as either the top of the `min_heap` or the average of the tops of both heaps.
